  "id": "gr-temoii",
  "connector": "〜てもいい",
  "gloss": "may; it’s OK to",
  "title": "〜てもいい — is it OK if…?",
  "pattern": "verb て form + もいい(ですか)",
  "explanation": "てもいい gives or asks permission: {座|すわ}ってもいいですか — may I sit down? Say yes with どうぞ, or いいですよ. With a negative, なくてもいい means “you don’t have to” (two lessons on).",
  "natural": "Asking politely in shops, homes and offices: {写真|しゃしん}を{撮|と}ってもいいですか; {窓|まど}を{開|あ}けてもいい？",
  "stiff": "Answering with だめです is very blunt. ちょっと…, or すみません、ここはちょっと…, is the usual soft no.",
  "examples": [
    {
